  <metadata>
    <description><![CDATA[{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 BLT ReaScripts & JSFX\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 BLT ReaScripts is a collection of workflow tools for REAPER. \u8251 ?\u946 ? version\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Installation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Install {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
 if it is not already installed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab In REAPER, open {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories...}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Paste the following repository URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/balrulu/reaper/raw/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Synchronize ReaPack, open {\b Browse packages...}, and search for {\f1 BLT}.\par}
